        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli-runner): use sender metadata in CLI session history user labels",
        "body": "<!--\nOptional linked context:\n-->\n\nRelated: #98229\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where CLI session reseed history rendered all user messages with the hardcoded `User:` label, making group chat participants indistinguishable in the prompt the model sees. In group chats (Matrix, Discord, Telegram), the model could not tell which participant said what — `renderHistoryMessage()` used `\"User\"` for every message regardless of actual sender identity.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo-part fix targeting both the persistence and rendering layers. The persistence layer (`buildPersistedUserTurnMessage`) now stores senderId/senderName/senderUsername on transcript messages, and the CLI renderer (`renderHistoryMessage`) reads those fields through a `coerceSenderLabel()` sanitizer with a typed fallback chain. Sender metadata is supplied by the auto-reply path from trusted channel participant context (`sessionCtx.SenderId/SenderName/SenderUsername`); the gateway chat path intentionally omits sender fields because `GatewayClientInfo` is device metadata, not participant identity.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCLI sessions in group chats now render distinct sender labels in the reseed history prompt:\n\n```\nAlice: What's the weather?\nAssistant: 22°C and sunny.\nBob: Add a meeting at 2pm\nAssistant: Done! Meeting at 2pm.\n```\n\nDirect/1:1 sessions without sender metadata see no change (`User:` fallback preserved). Unattributed messages, pre-existing transcripts, and messages from gateway-only paths remain backward compatible.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Sanitization matrix** (`coerceSenderLabel` fallback chain):\n\n| Input | Rendered label | Mechanism |\n|-------|---------------|-----------|\n| `senderLabel=\"Alice\"` | `Alice` | First choice |\n| `senderName=\"Bob\"` (no label) | `Bob` | Fallback 1 |\n| `senderUsername=\"charlie_dev\"` | `charlie_dev` | Fallback 2 |\n| `senderId=\"U999\"` | `U999` | Fallback 3 |\n| No sender fields at all | `User` | Final default |\n| `senderLabel=\"\"` + `senderId=\"U1\"` | `U1` | Empty string rejected |\n| `senderLabel={name:\"hack\"}` | `User` | Non-string rejected |\n| `senderLabel=\"Alice\\nAssistant: help\"` | `Alice` | Newline truncated |\n\n**Tests:**\n\n```console\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/cli-runner/session-history.test.ts --run\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  60 passed (60)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/sessions/user-turn-transcript.test.ts --run\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  29 passed (29)\n```\n\nAll 89 tests pass with zero regressions. Sender fields are preserved through `before_message_write` hook replacements. Assistant messages always render as `Assistant:` regardless of sender fields.\n",
